red Democrats by several points. Markets and the fundamentals align on a margin near 18 points.", "watch": "A late scandal or an unusually large national Democratic wave could narrow the margin, though the seat itself is very unlikely to flip.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Celeste Maloy (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Celeste Maloy is seeking a second full term in a southern and central Utah district that voted about 21 points Republican at the presidential level. She secured her party's nomination and enters the general election with a large financial edge, having raised roughly $1.7 million and drawn about $1.3 million in outside support, while Democratic nominee Kent Udell has raised under $100,000. Several independent and minor-party candidates are on the ballot but show little fundraising activity.\n\nThe only public poll, conducted in mid-September, gave Maloy a 19-point lead among likely voters, and prediction markets put her chances around 96 to 97 percent. Debates in the race have centered on public lands, nuclear energy, and affordability, but Udell has shown little capacity to close the gap in a district this red. The forecast rates the seat as safely Republican.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0155, "margin": -18.58}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0256, "margin": -18.6}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0177, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0181, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0129, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0141, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0181, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0196, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0119, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -18.4}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.016, "margin": -18.4}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0126, "margin": -18.0